ons and settings  and i hope the public as we have more  rats generally available will take  advantage of them because i i do believe  they're much more convenient done in the  calm of your home  and you have an answer within minutes  instead of waiting several days for the  pcr results  next question  your next question comes from richard  southern with city news 680 please go  ahead  hi premier good morning premier you said  at the beginning of the month that  restaurants gyms and movie theaters were  closing to protect hospitals can you  then tell us today why restaurants gyms  and movies are reopening before elective  surgery is resuming  well i'll just repeat what i  said earlier on richard  there was three areas of focus  number one  is when we we saw the  hospitalizations double every single  week  we saw the positivity rate go right up  to 40 percent  now we've seen it drop down to 15.9  percent and everyone saw the absenteeism  in your own workplace not to mention the  the health care sector you know we're  doing everything we can to make sure we  uh bolster the the health care system uh  keeping keep in mind folks i'm gonna go  back a little bit here the liberal  government fired sixteen hundred nurses  our health care system was not in good  shape uh when we took office since then  we've hired over six thousand seven  hundred health care workers we're going  to be bringing in another six thousand  in march we're putting billions and  billions of dollars  into the health care system we want to  make sure that we're prepared for any  future pandemic we've put in billion  tens of billions of dollars into  infrastructure and building new  hospitals right across this province and  we're going to continue to invest in our  health care but we can't do it alone no  province can do it alone  since i've been elected we've been on  the federal government for the cht the  canadian health transfers  we are paying as ontarians uh 78 of the  cost uh the federal government and it's  not just this federal government it's  prior federal governments i don't care  if it's conservative or liberal  they're pitching in 22  that's unacceptable every single premier  is in line with making sure that the  federal government pays their fair share  of health care and it's not one-time  funding that we're looking for we need  continuous funding non-stop until we can  hire more health care workers until we  can take care of our nurses until we can  continue uh bringing in new technology  and and building new hospitals but i can  tell you every single premier is in line  on this we're going to have a meeting  today with all the premiers we need the  federal government to step up it's very  simple we will not be able to move  forward not only as a province as a  country  with with the uh the federal government  pitching in 22  and putting the vast majority of the  burden on the backs of our of the  provinces  follow-up  okay follow up for dr moore dr moore  there's a letter posted online appearing  to be from you addressed to the niagara  region chief medical officer of health  in which you quote express concern with  measures he's taking with schools in  that region including weekly co2  monitoring in classrooms the dismissal  of cohorts if there's a positive case  and the use of medical exemption notes  for masks is that letter accurate sir  cannot local medical officers of health  make their own decisions and dr moore  what's so wrong with these measures  oh so we meet with our medical officers  health on a regular basis we have  consultation to them from this office to  local public health and i thank all the  local public health officials for all  their work they're doing to protect  the health of their communities both  through vaccination and case and contact  management and outbreak management  what i'm trying to have across ontario  is a consistent and persistent approach  so that parents school boards families  can expect the same level o